  "notes": [
    "A6 and A7 are analog inputs only. They have no digital driver, so digitalRead/digitalWrite do nothing on them, a surprise that costs people an afternoon.",
    "A4/A5 are the only I2C pins; D10-D13 are the SPI pins.",
    "VIN takes 7-12 V. The regulator is small, so a 12 V supply plus a few peripherals will get hot.",
    "Clones ship with a CH340 instead of the original FT232RL, which needs a different USB driver but is otherwise interchangeable.",
    "RESET appears twice on the header, which is handy when the ICSP side is occupied.",
    "The newer Nano Every, Nano 33 IoT and Nano ESP32 keep this footprint but have different peripherals. The Nano Every is still 5 V; the Nano 33 IoT and Nano ESP32 are 3.3 V parts."
  ],
